{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f009","f013"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=helper-param-null-deref; Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot for the cross-function form of the seed invariant: a netlink handler or dispatch core passes an attribute pointer (an info->attrs[N]/tb[N] slot, or a local variable holding it) as a function argument into a helper, and the callee dereferences the parameter (nla_get_*/nla_data/nla_len/nla_parse_nested*/nla_validate_nested*/nla_for_each_nested) without its own NULL check, while no caller-side presence guard or policy-required entry covers that exact attribute. Prioritize the surfaces prior s01 artifacts explicitly left unresolved: nf_conntrack_netlink tuple/help/expect-nat parse helpers, nf_nat_core parse helpers, the nft_ct and nfnetlink_cttimeout policy parsers, br_parse_vlan_tunnel_info, seg6_local parse_nla_bpf, net/ipv4/fou.c parse sites, and any dereference routed through an intermediate local (e.g. attr = info->attrs[N]) or helper macro that direct-index pattern scans missed. For each helper, enumerate its callers and prove with source evidence whether the attribute can be NULL for an attacker-crafted, userns-reachable genl/rtnl/nfnetlink message; candidates already reported for this snapshot (mac802154_hwsim.c handlers, nft_tunnel.c, net/mpls/af_mpls.c) must not be re-reported. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s01 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f010","f012"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=helper-param-null-deref; Search only snapshots/s02 and no other snapshot for the cross-function form of the seed invariant: an attribute pointer from an info->attrs[N]/tb[N] slot (or a local variable holding it) is passed as a function argument into a helper that dereferences the parameter (nla_get_*/nla_data/nla_len/nla_parse_nested*/nla_validate_nested*/nla_for_each_nested) without its own NULL check, while no caller-side presence guard or policy-required entry covers that exact attribute. Prioritize the surfaces prior s02 artifacts listed as unresolved or only spot-checked: nf_tables_api.c expression/element list helpers, openvswitch flow_netlink.c action parsers, ip_tunnel_core.c, seg6_local.c, nexthop.c, lwt_bpf.c, pmsr.c, team.c, qeth helpers, devlink helpers, and drbd_nla.c, plus slot dereferences routed through intermediate variables or helper macros that direct-index pattern scans missed. For each helper, enumerate its callers and prove with source evidence whether the attribute can be NULL for an attacker-crafted, userns-reachable message; candidates already reported for this snapshot (mac802154_hwsim.c, i40e_main.c and ice_main.c bridge setlink) must not be re-reported. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s02 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f002","f011"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=helper-param-null-deref; Search only snapshots/s03 and no other snapshot for the cross-function form of the seed invariant: an attribute pointer from an info->attrs[N]/tb[N] slot, or a local variable holding it, is passed into a helper (parse helper, callback, or macro wrapper) that dereferences the parameter (nla_get_*/nla_data/nla_len/nla_parse_nested*/nla_validate_nested*/nla_for_each_nested) without its own NULL check, while no caller-side presence guard or policy-required entry covers that exact attribute. Focus on the gap prior s03 artifacts flagged: parse/validate call sites whose nesting attribute or consumed attribute reaches the helper through an intermediate local or helper parameter rather than direct attrs[]/tb[] indexing, and attribute values that pass through intermediate locals before use; kernel-side dump/notify builders that only construct attributes are out of scope unless they parse user input. For each site, trace the data flow back to the originating handler and prove with source evidence whether the attribute can be NULL for an attacker-crafted, userns-reachable message; candidates already reported for this snapshot (mac802154_hwsim.c handlers) must not be re-reported, and an evidence-backed negative over this surface is a valid result. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s03 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f004","f013"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=kind-callback-tb-gaps; Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot for the seed invariant relocated into per-kind registered callbacks: a dispatch core parses a message into a tb[]/data[]/tca[] table under a policy that does not mark the consumed attributes required and hands it to a registered callback whose own guard is inverted, partial, or absent before it dereferences slots. Cover the surfaces prior s01 artifacts enumerated but did not deep-read: rtnl_link_ops per-kind .newlink/.changelink/.validate implementations (vxlan, geneve, macsec, gtp, bonding, ipvlan, hsr, xfrm_interface, ipoib and the tunnel kinds), net/sched per-qdisc/per-filter/per-action kind ->init()/->change() callbacks consuming tca[TCA_OPTIONS], and nf_tables expression/type ->init() callbacks beyond the already-reported nft_tunnel.c instance (nft_expr_init passes a tb[] parsed with each expression's own non-required policy into ops->init). For each callback record function, file:line, the guard or its absence, the dereferenced slot, the policy entry, and userns reachability of the dispatch path; candidates already reported for this snapshot must not be re-reported. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s01 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f003","f012"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=kind-callback-tb-gaps; Search only snapshots/s02 and no other snapshot for the seed invariant relocated into per-kind registered callbacks that consume caller-parsed attribute tables: the dispatch core (rtnetlink newlink/changelink, net/sched kind init/change, nf_tables nft_expr_init) parses into tb[]/data[]/tca[] under a policy that does not mark the consumed attributes required, and the registered callback dereferences a slot under an inverted, partial, or absent guard. First resolve the candidate a prior artifact flagged but never examined in this snapshot: net/netfilter/nft_tunnel.c nft_tunnel_get_init, which per cross-snapshot evidence carries 'if (!tb[NFTA_TUNNEL_KEY] && !tb[NFTA_TUNNEL_DREG]) return -EINVAL;' followed by unguarded nla_get_be32(tb[NFTA_TUNNEL_KEY]) and nft_parse_register(tb[NFTA_TUNNEL_DREG]) — record its exact line numbers here, the nft_tunnel_policy entries, and the nfnetlink/userns reachability. Then audit the ~60 rtnl_link_ops per-kind newlink/changelink handlers that were only pattern-grepped, the net/sched per-kind init/change callbacks, and the remaining nft expression/type init callbacks. Record function, file:line, guard, dereferenced slot, policy entry, and reachability; candidates already reported for this snapshot (mac802154_hwsim.c, i40e_main.c, ice_main.c) must not be re-reported. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s02 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f008","f011"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=kind-callback-tb-gaps; Search only snapshots/s03 and no other snapshot for the seed invariant relocated into per-kind registered callbacks that consume caller-parsed attribute tables: rtnl_link_ops kind callbacks, net/sched per-kind ->init()/->change() callbacks, ndo_fdb_add/ndo_fdb_del implementations, dcbnl per-table handlers, and nf_tables expression/type ->init() callbacks, where the core hands over tb[]/data[]/tca[] parsed under policies that do not mark the consumed attributes required and the callback dereferences a slot under an inverted, partial, or absent guard. Prioritize the surfaces the prior s03 rtnl artifact left unresolved: vxlan_nl2conf in drivers/net/vxlan.c (the sole attribute consumer of vxlan_changelink, never audited attribute-by-attribute), the 22 remaining .changelink implementations (bond_netlink.c, geneve.c, macsec.c, vlan_netlink.c, br_netlink.c, ip_gre/ip6_gre/ip6_tunnel/ip_vti/ipip/ip6_vti/sit, xfrm_interface, ipoib_netlink, rmnet_config, caif_hsi, chnl_net), and the ndo_fdb_add/ndo_fdb_del callback bodies beyond the NDA_LLADDR guarantee. Record function, file:line, guard, dereferenced slot, policy entry, and reachability; candidates already reported for this snapshot (mac802154_hwsim.c handlers) must not be re-reported. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s03 with execution_status, areas searched, candidates, or an evidence-backed negative."}
